,title,link,text,language,family
0,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.",Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of China - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_China,"April 28, 2026 - China has many ethnic groups besides the Han, who reside in various regions around the nation. These include Tibetans, Uyghurs, Manchus, Zhuang, Dai, Mongolians, Naxi, Miao, Wa, Yi, and Lisu.",Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
2,Lisu people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisu_people,"4 weeks ago - Linguistically, Lisu belong to the Yi language or Nuosu branch of the Sino-Tibetan family.",Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
3,"Lisu Ethnic Minority-Yunnan Tour, Yunnan Travel, Yunnan Travel Agency, Yunnan Trip, Yunnan Guide",https://www.yunnanexploration.com/lisu-ethnic-minority.html,"Lisu folk songs have a distinctive style. When singing short notes, they often use a vibrato, while longer notes are sung in a straightforward and simple manner. The tone is deep and resonant, creating a sense of inner strength.",Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
4,"Folk Songs of Lisu Ethnic Minority: Introduction, Feature, Instrument",https://www.yunnanexploration.com/folk-songs-of-lisu-ethnic-minority.html,"Lisu Ethnic Minority is a group good at singing and dancing, accompanied by the national instrument Qiben(其奔). Folk song of Lisu Ethnic Minority is very popular, which is reflected in the old saying that ""Salt is indispensable in meals, ...",Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
5,Lisu Traditional Music | norient.com,https://norient.com/stories/lisu-traditional-music,"The language of the Lisu belongs to the Tibeto-Burma branch, with no written system historically. Western missionary invented an alphabetical written form that is used mainly for bible reading. At the beginning of the 20th Century, one tribe tried to create a pictogram written form. Music is a vital element in the lives of the Lisus and music is performed in family gatherings, festivals, weddings, funerals, when they go hunting, herding, planting, harvesting, and even in resolving conflicts.",Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
6,Understanding the importance of Tibetan music,https://www.tibettravel.org/tibetan-culture/understanding-the-importance-of-tibetan-music.html,"May 6, 2025 - You will find that flutes and lutes combine with some percussion beats to create a soft aroma of music that is thought to resemble a constant communication link with the divine world, one that only ""perfect beings"" are able to compose. It is officially named Sino-Mongolian music and is heard in the streets during festivals and parties.",Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
7,"71-51 ROOF, DeLagnel Haigh, 1932- A GRAMMAR OF THE LISU LANGUAGE.","https://theswissbay.ch/pdf/Books/Linguistics/Mega+linguistics+pack/Sino-Tibetan/Lisu+Language,+A+Grammar+of+the+(Roop).pdf",A GRAMMAR OF THE LISU LANGUAGE.,Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
8,MUSIC IN TIBET | Facts and Details,https://factsanddetails.com/china/cat6/sub36/item206.html,Their songs and music are well-modulated in tone and the words fit well with the tunes.The areas inhabited by Tibetans boasts a great diversity of folk songs and dances. Some musical instruments were introduced from the interior of China. Long-handled drums and trumpets are the main musical instruments used by the lamas.,Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
9,Lisu in China people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/13076/ch,"Learn about the Lisu in China people group. Profiles include statistics, text, photo, map, progress indicator and language resources.",Lisu,Sino-Tibetan
